course: dictionary
lesson: 6174
title: The Minoans
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Minoan is a person from the Minoan civilisation, and «Minoan» is the word for anything to do with them. A civilisation is a whole society, with its own towns, art and ways of living. The Minoans lived on the Greek island of Crete from about 3000 to 1100 BC.
explain: Look at the clues in «On Crete the Minoans built the palace of Knossos with many rooms about 3,700 years ago.» Crete is an island, a palace is a huge home for rulers, and «years ago» tells you it is very old. So Minoan links a people to a place and a time. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A people or a place from long ago.
explain: Now look at «The Minotaur is a myth, but bull-leaping was a real sport or ritual of the Minoans.» The word «but» shows a contrast: the Minotaur is a made-up story, while bull-leaping was real. Minoan is not a myth. It names real people who lived and built things.
explain: The name comes from King Minos, a king in old legends. Historians use Minoan for the real civilisation on Crete, so when you read the word, think about real history.
fact: Minoan means to do with the Minoans, an ancient Bronze Age civilisation on Crete.
fact: A Minoan is a person from that civilisation, and the plural is Minoans.
fact: «Minoan palace» means a great palace, such as Knossos, built on Crete.
fact: «Minoan art» means pictures made by the Minoans, such as colourful wall pictures called frescoes of dolphins.
fact: The Minoans traded by sea, and their writing, Linear A, has still not been deciphered, so nobody can read it yet.
exercise: What is a Minoan? | *A person from the ancient civilisation on the Greek island of Crete | A monster that lived in a labyrinth | A modern Greek footballer | A king who ruled Athens today
exercise: «The Minotaur is a myth, but bull-leaping was a real sport or ritual of the Minoans.» Is the Minotaur real? | *No, it is a myth | Yes, it was painted on a wall of Crete | Yes, it lived in the palace of Knossos
exercise: Which word fits? «The Minoans built a great ____ at Knossos.» | bull | river | fish | *palace
test: The Minoans painted colourful wall pictures called what? | myths | labyrinths | kings | *frescoes
test: How did the Minoans trade? | by horse and cart | by rocket | by train | *by sea
exam: Which sentence uses Minoan correctly? | *Minoan art shows colourful dolphins painted on palace walls | I had a Minoan for breakfast | The Minoan bus leaves at nine every day | Minoan is a Greek word for a type of pizza
